 Runs lint, tests, and a scheduled CodeQL analysis.
 
-Actions are referenced by major version tag. There is no Dependabot configuration.
+## How action updates are handled
+
+Every action in `.github/workflows/` is pinned to a full commit SHA, with the
+release version in a trailing comment (for example `# v7.0.1`). Tags are mutable,
+so the SHA is what gets executed.
+
+Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) maintains these pins:
+
+- It checks the `github-actions` ecosystem weekly.
+- All action updates are grouped into a single pull request.
+- A 7-day cooldown delays brand-new releases, so a compromised release is likely
+  to be caught and yanked before we adopt it.
+- Dependabot rewrites both the SHA and the version comment.
+
+Review each update pull request by reading the upstream diff between the old and
+new SHA, not just the version number, then merge it. Do not edit pins by hand or
+switch back to tag references; Dependabot expects the `# vX.Y.Z` comment.
+
+Current pins: `actions/checkout` v7.0.1, `astral-sh/setup-uv` v10.3.2 (v10.3.3 was
+inside the cooldown window when pinned), `github/codeql-action` v4.39.1.
